@verbs columns rows terminal sidebar screen
@tier player
@title fitting the game to the size of your screen
@see quit

The game lays its text out by how wide you tell it your screen is,
so it is worth setting once.

  columns [<number>]

With no number, it says how many you have now. With one, it
changes them; it has to be between 35 and 200. You start at 80.

  rows <number>

How many lines fit at a time, for the pauses when reading long
texts. It has to be more than ten. You start at 25.

  terminal <type>

What your terminal can do, colour above all. A type that does not
exist is refused, but you are not shown the list.

  sidebar <on|off>

Draws a panel down the right of the screen with a map and your
health and energy bars. It needs a terminal that understands cursor
positioning, and the room for it is taken from the last twelve of
the columns you declared.
